{"type":"item.started","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show d723f616fa903bd37c2140cbb86651161f94c47b:attest/specs/212/spec.md | sed -n '1,220p'; sed -n '320,440p' attavo/build.py; sed -n '220,300p' tests/test_adapters.py; sed -n '235,285p' tests/test_executor_conformance.py; git diff d723f616fa903bd37c2140cbb86651161f94c47b..22d65cf7f95ce91272d0453ea691699c03d69ef9 -- attest/specs/212/spec.md attest/specs/212/criteria\"","aggregated_output":"","exit_code":null,"status":"in_progress"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_7","type":"command_execution","command":"/bin/zsh -lc \"git show d723f616fa903bd37c2140cbb86651161f94c47b:attest/specs/212/spec.md | sed -n '1,220p'; sed -n '320,440p' attavo/build.py; sed -n '220,300p' tests/test_adapters.py; sed -n '235,285p' tests/test_executor_conformance.py; git diff d723f616fa903bd37c2140cbb86651161f94c47b..22d65cf7f95ce91272d0453ea691699c03d69ef9 -- attest/specs/212/spec.md attest/specs/212/criteria\"","aggregated_output":"git: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-M7dX6t5d' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-eDlmryj0' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n## Problem\n\nA build spends most of its time running the whole test suite, three times, around the executor's work. Read from #194's `build-01`: 215 s before the executor began, where `attavo build` runs `[checks].command` whole only to learn whether it can run at all (exit 2) and the feed shows nothing; 241 s at the gate, the whole suite again; and a 590 s wait inside the executor on a third run, because the instruction names the tenant's checks command and an executor given a command runs it (tenant zero's build-10 earned the present wording, \"are run for you\"; it did not stop #194, #204, or #206, where the suite was run twice inside one build). About 1,050 s of suite around 220 s of work, ahead of a required `test` check on the forge that runs the same suite and that the item waits on before review in any case.\n\nThe operator ruled four changes on 2026-09-20.\n\n1. The question asked before the first build is answered by a probe the tenant declares: `[checks].probe`, run once inside `[checks].probe_timeout_s` (required with it), exit 0 meaning this machine can run the checks and anything else, or the bound, an environment refusal written as today's is. A tenant with no probe is asked the old way. Either way the feed says \"checking this machine can run the checks\" before and the answer after.\n2. The executor is given one test command, `attavo test N` (`ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND`, with `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` when the tenant declares `[tests].call_timeout_s`): it selects, through the tenant's `[tests].select`, for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not, the records directory aside; runs them through `[tests].run`; exits as the run does; and at the bound ends the run with everything it started and exits 124. `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` leaves the contract and the instruction; the instruction says not to run the whole suite or any whole-tree check.\n3. One definition of the checks, split by where each runs: this repository's gate (`[checks].command`) runs the type check, which is fast and which the forge also requires (#206's `build-01` passed a gate that did not run it and left the head red); the whole suite runs once, as the forge's required `test` check. Until the reconciler's R3 returns a build whose head a required check rejects, a suite failure the selected tests missed costs the operator a Rebuild, which the operator accepted.\n4. This repository's selector maps a module to its own tests and fails safe: a path it does not know selects the whole suite; a test file selects itself; prose and the repository's own specs and records select nothing.\n\nThe stub under `stub/` is thin by the operator's ruling: `attavo test` sees committed changes only and ends nothing it started, the probe has no bound and no feed lines, the selector knows one module, and ten of the thirteen tests in `tests/test_testtool.py` fail on it. Three tests in `tests/test_self_tenancy.py` pinned the old selector and the suite in the gate; the stub carries them as they must read after this item. `python3 -m mypy` exits 0 on the built tree with no `type: ignore`; the builder runs it last, after its final change to any file. The builder does not run the whole suite.\n\nRetires: the whole run of the checks before a build where a tenant declares a probe; `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` and the sentence that named it; the whole suite in this repository's `[checks].command`; the selector's `bin/attavo` row and its silence on `attavo/**`.\n\n## Claims\n\n- attavo/build.py\n- attavo/testtool.py\n- attavo/cli.py\n- adapters/claude-code/run\n- adapters/codex/run\n- adapters/README.md\n- adapters/claude-code/README.md\n- adapters/codex/README.md\n- adapters/*/conformance.json\n- schema/manifest.schema.json\n- attavo.toml\n- .attavo/bin/select-tests\n- README.md\n- tests/test_testtool.py\n- tests/test_executor_conformance.py\n- tests/test_adapters.py\n- tests/test_adapters_codex.py\n- tests/test_adapter_claude_code.py\n- tests/test_adapter_codex.py\n- tests/test_build.py\n- tests/test_cli_help.py\n- tests/test_self_tenancy.py\n- tests/test_record_schemas.py\n\n## Criteria\n\n- build-asks-the-probe-and-not-the-whole-checks.sh: with a probe declared, one build runs the probe once and the checks once (at its gate, not before it); with a probe that exits 3 the build is refused as an environment stop and the executor never runs\n- attavo-test-runs-the-selected-tests-inside-a-bound.sh: attavo test 1 hands the run exactly what the tenant's select names for the item's changed paths, exits 7 when the run does, and exits 124 within seconds when the run outlasts a 2 s call_timeout_s\n- the-selector-fails-safe-and-the-gate-drops-the-suite.sh: this repository's selector answers tests for a module it does not know, tests/test_report.py for attavo/report.py, and nothing for prose and records; attavo.toml's gate command runs the type check and not the suite, and declares a probe with its bound and a call_timeout_s\n- the-executor-is-given-one-test-command.sh: ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND is named nowhere in attavo/build.py or either real adapter, ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND is named in all three, the manifest schema carries probe (requiring probe_timeout_s with it) and call_timeout_s, tests/test_testtool.py carries its thirteen tests by name, and the conformance suite carries situation 7 under its new name\n                \"halted\": None,\n                \"stop\": {\"class\": \"environment\", \"provenance\": \"tenant\", \"detail\": detail},\n            }\n            record_path = write_record(item_records_dir, \"build\", record, m, item_id,\n                                       log=log or refusal_text + \"\\n\")\n            print(f\"attavo build: refused ({record_path.name})\")\n            return 1\n        append_event(events_path, \"gate\", \"this machine can run the checks\")\n\n    adapter_version = model = model_version = None\n    tokens = {\"input\": 0, \"output\": 0}\n    cost_usd = None\n    transcripts: list[str] = []\n    criteria_results: list[dict[str, Any]] = []\n    selected_tests: dict[str, Any] | None = None\n    checks_result: dict[str, Any] | None = None\n    status_out = \"failed\"\n    refusal = None\n    refusal_provenance = None\n    halted = None\n    iterations_used = 0\n\n    with tempfile.TemporaryDirectory() as tmp:\n        feedback_path = Path(tmp) / \"feedback.txt\"\n        feedback_path.write_text(\"\")\n\n        for iteration in range(1, BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET + 1):\n            iterations_used = iteration\n            append_event(events_path, \"iteration\", f\"iteration {iteration} of {BUILD_ITERATION_BUDGET}\")\n            env = dict(os.environ)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR\"] = str(spec_dir)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR\"] = str(item_records_dir)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_RULINGS\"] = str(root / m[\"paths\"][\"rulings\"])\n            env[\"ATTAVO_BRANCH\"] = branch\n            env[\"ATTAVO_ITERATION\"] = str(iteration)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_FEEDBACK\"] = str(feedback_path)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG\"] = json.dumps(adapter_config)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_STAGE\"] = \"build\"\n            env[\"ATTAVO_EVENTS\"] = str(events_path)\n            env[\"ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND\"] = f\"python3 {PRODUCT_ROOT / 'bin' / 'attavo'} test {item_id}\"\n            if tests_cfg.get(\"call_timeout_s\"):\n                env[\"ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S\"] = str(tests_cfg[\"call_timeout_s\"])\n            else:\n                env.pop(\"ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S\", None)\n            env[\"GIT_AUTHOR_NAME\"] = identity[\"name\"]\n            env[\"GIT_AUTHOR_EMAIL\"] = identity[\"email\"]\n            env[\"GIT_COMMITTER_NAME\"] = identity[\"name\"]\n            env[\"GIT_COMMITTER_EMAIL\"] = identity[\"email\"]\n\n            run = subprocess.run([str(adapter_path)], cwd=str(root), env=env,\n                                 capture_output=True, text=True, check=False)\n            transcript, payload = split_adapter_stdout(run.stdout)\n            if run.returncode != 0:\n                # The guarantee behind issue #53's refusal: an adapter that\n                # exits non-zero always leaves a non-empty log, even one\n                # that printed nothing at all on stderr.\n                detail = f\"[adapter exited {run.returncode}]\"\n                if run.stderr.strip():\n                    detail += \"\\n\" + run.stderr.rstrip(\"\\n\")\n                transcript = (transcript + \"\\n\" if transcript else \"\") + detail\n            transcripts.append(transcript)\n\n            if run.returncode != 0 or payload is None or not payload.get(\"model\"):\n                status_out = \"failed\"\n                break\n\n            adapter_version = payload.get(\"adapter_version\")\n            model = payload.get(\"model\")\n            model_version = payload.get(\"model_version\")\n            tok = payload.get(\"tokens\") or {}\n            tokens[\"input\"] += tok.get(\"input\", 0) or 0\n            tokens[\"output\"] += tok.get(\"output\", 0) or 0\n            iter_cost = payload.get(\"cost_usd\")\n            if iter_cost is not None:\n                cost_usd = (cost_usd or 0) + iter_cost\n\n            if payload.get(\"status\") == \"question\":\n                status_out = \"halted\"\n                halted = {\"question\": payload.get(\"question\")}\n                break\n\n            foreign = next((c for c in commits_since(root, start_sha)\n                           if c[\"name\"] != identity[\"name\"] or c[\"email\"] != identity[\"email\"]),\n                          None)\n            if foreign:\n                status_out = \"refused\"\n                refusal = f\"commit {foreign['sha']} not authored by the executor\"\n                break\n\n            protected = protected_path_touched(root, start_sha, records_rel, specs_rel)\n            if protected:\n                status_out = \"refused\"\n                refusal = protected\n                refusal_provenance = \"executor\"\n                break\n\n            touched = sorted(changed_paths(root, start_sha, records_rel))\n            bad_path = next((p for p in touched if not matches_a_claim(p, claims)), None)\n            if bad_path:\n                status_out = \"refused\"\n                refusal = bad_path\n                break\n\n            criteria_results = [\n                {\"name\": name, \"exit\": run_criterion(spec_dir / \"criteria\" / name, root)}\n                for name in criteria_names]\n            for c in criteria_results:\n                append_event(events_path, \"gate\", f\"{c['name']}: exit {c['exit']}\")\n\n            select_in = \"\".join(p + \"\\n\" for p in touched)\n            select_run = subprocess.run(tests_cfg[\"select\"], shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                                        input=select_in, capture_output=True,\n                                        text=True, check=False)\n            identifiers = [l for l in select_run.stdout.splitlines() if l.strip()]\n            run_in = \"\".join(i + \"\\n\" for i in identifiers)\n            test_run = subprocess.run(tests_cfg[\"run\"], shell=True, cwd=str(root),\n                                      input=run_in, capture_output=True,\n                                      text=True, check=False)\n            selected_tests = {\"select\": tests_cfg[\"select\"], \"run\": tests_cfg[\"run\"],\n                              \"count\": len(identifiers), \"exit\": test_run.returncode}\n\n    assert run.returncode == 1\n    assert \"allowed_tools\" in run.stderr\n\n\ndef test_claude_code_model_from_config(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Acceptance 4. model in the table appears as --model; the retired\n    ATTAVO_MODEL, even if still set in the environment, is ignored.\"\"\"\n    cmd = dry_run(tmp_path, config={\"model\": \"claude-sonnet-5\"},\n                 extra_env={\"ATTAVO_MODEL\": \"should-be-ignored\"})\n\n    assert cmd.count(\"--model\") == 1\n    assert cmd[cmd.index(\"--model\") + 1] == \"claude-sonnet-5\"\n    assert \"should-be-ignored\" not in cmd\n\n\ndef test_claude_code_names_the_tenants_checks(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Issue #30, acceptance 5, reworded by issue #36. The instruction\n    must not tell the executor to run the check itself. Regression:\n    build-10 on tenant zero, where \"must exit 0 before you commit\" made\n    the executor the runner (146 and 123 turns, 72 of 83 executor\n    minutes waiting on tools) of a check attavo build already runs after\n    every commit.\n\n    The command's mere presence in the instruction (with it, and its\n    absence without it) is now tests/test_executor_conformance.py's\n    situation 7 -- general across any adapter. What stays here is the\n    part that is an assertion about English and does not transfer.\n    \"\"\"\n    with_tool = dry_run(tmp_path, extra_env={\n        \"ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND\": \"python3 /product/bin/attavo test 7\"})\n    instruction = with_tool[with_tool.index(\"-p\") + 1]\n    assert \"are run for you\" in instruction\n    assert \"before you commit\" not in instruction\n    assert \"Do not run the whole test suite\" in instruction\n\n    without_tool = dry_run(tmp_path)\n    instruction_without = without_tool[without_tool.index(\"-p\") + 1]\n    assert \"are run for you\" not in instruction_without\n\n\ndef test_claude_code_adapter_derives_model_from_usage_breakdown(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The real response shape: no top-level \"model\", one modelUsage key.\"\"\"\n    response = {\n        \"is_error\": False,\n        \"structured_output\": {\"status\": \"done\", \"question\": None},\n        \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 5, \"output_tokens\": 9},\n        \"total_cost_usd\": 0.01,\n        \"modelUsage\": {\n            \"claude-sonnet-5\": {\"inputTokens\": 5, \"outputTokens\": 9},\n        },\n    }\n    run = run_with_response(tmp_path, response)\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stderr\n    line = json.loads(run.stdout.splitlines()[-1])\n    assert line[\"model\"] == \"claude-sonnet-5\"\n\n\ndef test_claude_code_adapter_derives_model_from_dominant_usage_key(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Several modelUsage keys (a lightweight helper model alongside the\n    primary one): the key with the most total tokens wins.\"\"\"\n    response = {\n        \"is_error\": False,\n        \"structured_output\": {\"status\": \"done\", \"question\": None},\n        \"usage\": {\"input_tokens\": 907, \"output_tokens\": 21},\n        \"total_cost_usd\": 0.05,\n        \"modelUsage\": {\n            \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\": {\"inputTokens\": 897, \"outputTokens\": 12},\n            \"claude-sonnet-5\": {\"inputTokens\": 10, \"outputTokens\": 9},\n        },\n    }\n    run = run_with_response(tmp_path, response)\n    assert run.returncode == 0, run.stderr\n    line = json.loads(run.stdout.splitlines()[-1])\n    assert line[\"model\"] == \"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001\"\n\n\ndef test_claude_code_adapter_fails_without_a_model_id(tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"No top-level \"model\" and empty modelUsage: the adapter must fail\n    loudly rather than emit an empty model that would let a \"pass\" record\n    through with no identity behind it. The raw result still reaches\n    stdout (issue #34) -- only the final report line is withheld.\"\"\"\n\n    env = base_env(tmp_path)\n    env[\"PATH\"] = f\"{fake_bin}{os.pathsep}{env.get('PATH', '')}\"\n\n    run = run_adapter(adapter_name, env)\n    assert run.returncode == 3\n    assert \"tool stdout: ran out of budget\" in run.stdout\n    assert \"tool stderr: overloaded_error\" in run.stdout\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\ndef test_situation_6_transcript_non_empty_on_every_path(adapter_name: str, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    for situation in (\"done\", \"is_error\", \"no_structured_output\", \"question_short\"):\n        run = run_situation(adapter_name, situation, tmp_path)\n        assert run.stdout.strip(), f\"{situation} produced no transcript at all\"\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\ndef test_situation_7_the_one_test_command_in_the_invocation(adapter_name: str, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"The executor is given one test command and no whole-tree command.\n    Naming the tenant's checks in the instruction made the executor their\n    runner however the sentence was worded (tenant zero build-10; #194's\n    590 s wait; #204 and #206, where the whole suite was run twice inside\n    one build), so the checks command is not in the instruction at all.\"\"\"\n    command = \"python3 /product/bin/attavo test 7\"\n    checks = \"python3 bin/factory-lane check --base origin/main\"\n    given = dry_run(adapter_name, tmp_path, extra_env={\n        \"ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND\": command, \"ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S\": \"240\",\n        \"ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND\": checks})\n    assert command in given[\"instruction\"]\n    assert \"240 s\" in given[\"instruction\"]\n    assert checks not in given[\"instruction\"]\n\n    without = dry_run(adapter_name, tmp_path)\n    assert command not in without[\"instruction\"]\n    assert \"attavo test\" not in without[\"instruction\"]\n\n\n@pytest.mark.parametrize(\"adapter_name\", ADAPTER_NAMES)\ndef test_situation_8_commits_carry_the_attavo_build_identity(adapter_name: str, tmp_path: Path) -> None:\n    \"\"\"Issue #33. attavo build exports the executor identity -- set by the\n    product, never the tenant's git config -- as GIT_AUTHOR_NAME/EMAIL and\n    GIT_COMMITTER_NAME/EMAIL before invoking the adapter; the adapter must\n    pass it through rather than setting its own explicit environment for\n    the underlying tool. The fake tool_binary here commits for real, so\n    this checks the adapter's own subprocess call, not just the harness.\n    Regression: the specimen is attavo/code-factory@e22fa85, an executor\n    commit indistinguishable in git log from the operator's own, because\n    no identity was exported for it to carry.\n    \"\"\"\n    manifest = CONFORMANCE[adapter_name]\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-plmNR7BB' (errno=Operation not permitted)\ngit: warning: confstr() failed with code 5: couldn't get path of DARWIN_USER_TEMP_DIR; using /tmp instead\ngit: error: couldn't create cache file '/tmp/xcrun_db-IZB5SKdr' (errno=Operation not permitted)\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
