stion\\\": null},\\n27:`attavo build N` refuses (exit 1, naming the cause, no record) unless the manifest declares `[executor].build` and `[tests].select` and `[tests].run`, and unless `attavo approval-status` would print `valid`. It invokes the named adapter — `adapters/<name>/run`, resolved first under the tenant's own `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/` — with the spec, the corpus, and the branch. After each return it checks that every path the adapter touched matches a spec claim, then runs the criteria against the tree, the tests `[tests].select` and `[tests].run` name for the touched paths, and — when the manifest declares `[checks].command` — the tenant's own whole-tree check, from the tenant root. `pass` requires every criterion, the test run, and the tenant's checks (if declared) to exit 0; a non-zero exit anywhere iterates, with the failure as feedback, up to a fixed budget. `[checks]` is optional; a tenant that declares none is not refused, unlike `[tests]`. A `question` from the adapter halts the loop at once (exit 3); nothing answers it in Phase 2. Every run writes the next `build-NN.json`, with the adapter's transcript beside it as `build-NN.log`. Nothing dispatches build; it is typed by the operator. The full contract is in the Phase 2 issue.\",\"is_error\":false}]},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"8327c9db-455b-4a76-8736-ba592c30dfef\",\"uuid\":\"f80614a2-f026-4dbf-b869-fb7dd3792bdb\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-21T01:42:47.245Z\",\"tool_use_result\":{\"stdout\":\"# Adapters\\n\\nAn adapter is an executable at `adapters/<name>/run`, resolved first under\\nthe tenant's `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/`.\\n`attavo build` invokes it with the tenant root as its working directory.\\n\\n## Environment\\n\\n- `ATTAVO_SPEC_DIR` — the work item's spec directory (`spec.md`, `criteria/`, `stub/`).\\n- `ATTAVO_RECORDS_DIR` — the work item's own records directory.\\n- `ATTAVO_RULINGS` — the tenant's rulings fi