",\"-own specs and records to the whole suite. The table of modules and their\",\"-tests, a test file selecting itself, and the adapters, schema, and templates\",\"-prefixes are the build's to write. tests/test_testtool.py fails on it.\\\"\\\"\\\"\",\"+\\\"\\\"\\\"select-tests: [tests].select for attavo build/verify/test (issue #103,\",\"+made fail-safe by issue #212).\",\"+\",\"+Reads changed paths on stdin, one per line, and prints test identifiers\",\"+on stdout, one per line, for this repository's own test suite:\",\"+\",\"+  - prose (*.md, LICENSE) and this repository's own specs and records\",\"+    (attest/specs/**, attest/records/**) select nothing;\",\"+  - a test file (tests/test_*.py) selects itself, and nothing at all when\",\"+    it no longer exists;\",\"+  - a path in MODULE_TESTS (a module of attavo/, and the few files that\",\"+    are one thing's own) selects the tests written for it, and a prefix in\",\"+    PREFIX_TESTS (adapters/, schema/, templates/) the tests written for\",\"+    that directory;\",\"+  - a path this selector does not know -- a module nobody mapped,\",\"+    bin/attavo, scripts/, tests/helpers.py and the fixtures every test\",\"+    stands on, the fixture adapter every build test invokes -- selects the\",\"+    whole suite (\\\"tests\\\", the one path pytest needs to run everything),\",\"+    and one such path is enough to make that the whole answer.\",\"+\",\"+A module that most of the others import (common, records, spec, ...) is\",\"+left out of MODULE_TESTS on purpose: no table of tests-per-module can know\",\"+what it breaks, so it is the whole suite. The forge runs the whole suite\",\"+once, as the required `test` check, in any case.\",\"+\",\"+Usage: <changed paths> | select-tests\",\"+\\\"\\\"\\\"\",\" from __future__ import annotations\",\" \",\" import sys\",\"+from pathlib import Path\",\" \",\"+ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\",\" \",\"+WHOLE_SUITE = \\\"tests\\\"\",\"+\",\"+SILENT_PREFIXES = (\