ns = open(p).read()\\ns = s.replace('ROOT = Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\\\\n\\\\n', '')\\ns = s.replace('''def is_prose_or_record''', '''def repository_root() -> Path:\\n    return Path(__file__).resolve().parent.parent.parent\\n\\n\\ndef is_prose_or_record''')\\ns = s.replace(\\\"(ROOT / path).is_file()\\\", \\\"(repository_root() / path).is_file()\\\")\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\nfor p in attavo/report.py attavo/common.py README.md attest/records/1/x.json bin/attavo scripts/a.py tests/test_ledger.py tests/test_gone.py tests/helpers.py adapters/codex/run adapters/fixture/run; do echo \\\"$p -> $(echo $p | python3 .attavo/bin/select-tests | tr '\\\\n' ' ')\\\"; done; git remote -v; git symbolic-ref -q refs/remotes/origin/HEAD\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01HB6Gt8wzuGYVccHyeWyndR\":{\"cwd\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-212\"}}}\n240:{\"type\":\"assistant\",\"message\":{\"model\":\"claude-sonnet-5\",\"id\":\"msg_011CfFjvvRVAsJwfQvDJVsCx\",\"type\":\"message\",\"role\":\"assistant\",\"content\":[{\"type\":\"tool_use\",\"id\":\"toolu_01TYDQtfnMZNv8g1irTHBmEH\",\"name\":\"Bash\",\"input\":{\"command\":\"python3 - <<'EOF'\\np = \\\"attavo/cli.py\\\"\\ns = open(p).read()\\nold = '''budget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\\nrefused. It writes the next build-NN.json'''\\nnew = '''budget. [checks] is optional; a tenant that declares none is not\\nrefused. Before the adapter is invoked it asks whether this machine can\\nrun the checks -- of [checks].probe, run once inside [checks].probe_timeout_s\\n(exit 0 yes; anything else, or the bound, an environment refusal), or,\\nfor a tenant that declares no probe, by running [checks].command whole\\n(exit 2 no) -- and says both the question and the answer in the feed\\n(issue #212). The adapter is given ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND, `attavo test N`,\\nand ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S when [tests].call_timeout_s is declared; it\\nis not given the tenant's checks. It writes the next build-NN.json'''\\nassert old in s\\ns = s.replace(old, new, 1)\\nold2 = '''verify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has'''\\nnew2 = '''test [N] runs the tests [tests].select names for every path the item has\\nchanged since it left the default branch (refs/remotes/origin/HEAD),\\ncommitted or not and untracked included, paths.records aside, through\\n[tests].run. It prints how many were selected (or that none was, and runs\\nnothing), exits as the run does, and, when [tests].call_timeout_s is\\ndeclared and the run outlasts it, ends the run and everything it started\\nand exits 124. It exits 2 when it cannot name the changes or the selector\\nfails. It is the one test command an executor is given (issue #212).\\n\\nverify refuses (exit 1) unless the item's latest build record has'''\\nassert old2 in s\\ns = s.replace(old2, new2, 1)\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\n\\n# adapters README\\np = \\\"adapters/README.md\\\"\\ns = open(p).read()\\nold = [l for l in s.splitlines() if l.startswith(\\\"- `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND`\\\")][0]\\nnew = (\\\"- `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` — build only: the one test command the executor is given, `attavo test <N>` (issue #212). It runs the tests the tenant's `[tests].select` names for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not, through `[tests].run`, and exits as the run does. An adapter tells the executor to run it while working, and not to run the whole test suite or any whole-tree check: the tenant's `[checks].command` is run at the gate after every commit, and a command the executor is named is a command the executor runs (#194's build-01 waited 590 s on the suite inside the executor). The tenant's checks command is not part of the contract.\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"- `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` — build only, set with `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` when the tenant declares `[tests].call_timeout_s`: the seconds one `attavo test` run is given before it is ended and exits 124. An adapter says so in the same sentence; absent, it says nothing about a bound.\\\")\\ns = s.replace(old, new)\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\n\\np = \\\"adapters/claude-code/README.md\\\"\\ns = open(p).read()\\ni = s.index(\\\"## The tenant's checks\\\")\\nj = s.index(\\\"## The sandbox is the boundary\\\")\\ns = s[:i] + '''## The tenant's tests\\n\\n`attavo build` runs the tenant's gates after each commit and feeds a\\nfailure back on the next iteration — the executor is not the runner of the\\ntenant's checks, and is not told what they are. When `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND`\\nis set (`../README.md`), the instruction gives it: \\\"to run tests while you\\nwork, run `<command>`: it runs the tests selected for the files you have\\nchanged and stops at `<N>` s. Do not run the whole test suite or any\\nwhole-tree check yourself: after you commit, the gates are run for you and\\nany failure is returned to you on the next iteration.\\\" The \\\"stops at\\\" clause\\nis present only when `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` is set. When\\n`ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` is unset, the instruction says nothing about tests.\\n\\n''' + s[j:]\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\ngit diff adapters/README.md | head -20; sed -n 40,70p adapters/codex/README.md; grep -n \\\"instruction\\\" adapters/codex/README.md | head\"},\"caller\":{\"type\":\"direct\"}}],\"container\":null,\"stop_reason\":null,\"stop_sequence\":null,\"stop_details\":null,\"usage\":{\"input_tokens\":2,\"cache_creation_input_tokens\":963,\"cache_read_input_tokens\":108645,\"cache_creation\":{\"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens\":0,\"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens\":963},\"output_tokens\":16,\"service_tier\":\"standard\",\"inference_geo\":\"not_available\"},\"input_transformations\":[],\"diagnostics\":null,\"context_management\":null},\"parent_tool_use_id\":null,\"session_id\":\"8327c9db-455b-4a76-8736-ba592c30dfef\",\"uuid\":\"5d587c31-ff6b-4c2e-9a69-db5b07bce585\",\"timestamp\":\"2026-09-21T01:46:57.411Z\",\"request_id\":\"req_011CfFjvuzgstnZnFuzdkrLk\",\"wire_tool_i