ND`\\\")][0]\\nnew = (\\\"- `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` — build only: the one test command the executor is given, `attavo test <N>` (issue #212). It runs the tests the tenant's `[tests].select` names for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not, through `[tests].run`, and exits as the run does. An adapter tells the executor to run it while working, and not to run the whole test suite or any whole-tree check: the tenant's `[checks].command` is run at the gate after every commit, and a command the executor is named is a command the executor runs (#194's build-01 waited 590 s on the suite inside the executor). The tenant's checks command is not part of the contract.\\\\n\\\"\\n       \\\"- `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` — build only, set with `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` when the tenant declares `[tests].call_timeout_s`: the seconds one `attavo test` run is given before it is ended and exits 124. An adapter says so in the same sentence; absent, it says nothing about a bound.\\\")\\ns = s.replace(old, new)\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\n\\np = \\\"adapters/claude-code/README.md\\\"\\ns = open(p).read()\\ni = s.index(\\\"## The tenant's checks\\\")\\nj = s.index(\\\"## The sandbox is the boundary\\\")\\ns = s[:i] + '''## The tenant's tests\\n\\n`attavo build` runs the tenant's gates after each commit and feeds a\\nfailure back on the next iteration — the executor is not the runner of the\\ntenant's checks, and is not told what they are. When `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND`\\nis set (`../README.md`), the instruction gives it: \\\"to run tests while you\\nwork, run `<command>`: it runs the tests selected for the files you have\\nchanged and stops at `<N>` s. Do not run the whole test suite or any\\nwhole-tree check yourself: after you commit, the gates are run for you and\\nany failure is returned to you on the next iteration.\\\" The \\\"stops at\\\" clause\\nis present only when `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` is set. When\\n`ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` is unset, the instruction says nothing about tests.\\n\\n''' + s[j:]\\nopen(p, \\\"w\\\").write(s)\\nEOF\\ngit diff adapters/README.md | head -20; sed -n 40,70p adapters/codex/README.md; grep -n \\\"instruction\\\" adapters/codex/README.md | head\"}},\"wire_ingest_context\":{\"toolu_01TYDQtfnMZNv8g1irTHBmEH\":{\"cwd\":\"/Users/davidbean/Projects/attavo-worktree-212\"}}}\n241:{\"type\":\"user\",\"message\":{\"role\":\"user\",\"content\":[{\"tool_use_id\":\"toolu_01TYDQtfnMZNv8g1irTHBmEH\",\"type\":\"tool_result\",\"content\":\"diff --git a/adapters/README.md b/adapters/README.md\\nindex bf06683..7148371 100644\\n--- a/adapters/README.md\\n+++ b/adapters/README.md\\n@@ -13,7 +13,8 @@ the tenant's `attavo/adapters/`, then under this product's `adapters/`.\\n - `ATTAVO_ITERATION` — the 1-based attempt number within this `attavo build` invocation.\\n - `ATTAVO_FEEDBACK` — a file holding the previous iteration's failing criteria, test output, and checks output; empty on the first iteration.\\n - `ATTAVO_ADAPTER_CONFIG` — the tenant manifest's `[executor.<adapter-name>]` table, serialized as JSON (`{}` when the tenant declared none). The product does not know what an adapter's settings mean; each adapter documents its own keys on its own `README.md`. **Never put a secret in this table** — it is copied verbatim into `build-NN.json` as `adapter_config`, and a record is not where secrets live.\\n-- `ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND` — the tenant's `[checks].command`, unset when the tenant declared no `[checks]` table. The product does not know what it checks; the tenant does. An adapter should tell the executor it is part of done when set, and say nothing about checks when it is not.\\n+- `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` — build only: the one test command the executor is given, `attavo test <N>` (issue #212). It runs the tests the tenant's `[tests].select` names for every path the item has changed since it left the default branch, committed or not, through `[tests].run`, and exits as the run does. An adapter tells the executor to run it while working, and not to run the whole test suite or any whole-tree check: the tenant's `[checks].command` is run at the gate after every commit, and a command the executor is named is a command the executor runs (#194's build-01 waited 590 s on the suite inside the executor). The tenant's checks command is not part of the contract.\\n+- `ATTAVO_TEST_TIMEOUT_S` — build only, set with `ATTAVO_TEST_COMMAND` when the tenant declares `[tests].call_timeout_s`: the seconds one `attavo test` run is given before it is ended and exits 124. An adapter says so in the same sentence; absent, it says nothing about a bound.\\n - `ATTAVO_STAGE` — `\\\"build\\\"`, `\\\"verify\\\"`, or `\\\"counsel\\\"` (issue #100), which invocation this is. An adapter that supports every stage branches on it; one that only builds may ignore it.\\n - `ATTAVO_EVENTS` — build and verify only: a file path an adapter may append events to while it runs (issue #26). Absent on a stage that does not set it (counsel does not); an adapter that never checks for it breaks nothing.\\n - `ATTAVO_DIFF` — verify only: a file holding the diff since the build's approval.\\n- `--json` prints one JSON object per stdout line (JSONL): `thread.started`,\\n  `turn.started`, `item.*`, and a terminal `turn.completed` (carrying\\n  `usage`) or `turn.failed`. codex's own exit code is 1 on `turn.failed`,\\n  0 on `turn.completed` -- read directly, so this adapter reads the\\n  terminal event for the reason, not for the verdict.\\n- `--output-schema <FILE>` plus `--output-last-message <FILE>` writes the\\n  final response as one JSON object once the turn completes -- this is\\n  where `findings`/`tests_named` (verify) or `status`/`question` (build)\\n  come from.\\n\\n## Events (issue #138)\\n\\nWith `ATTAVO_EVENTS` set, each `item.completed` line on the `--json`\\nstream maps to `../README.md`'s shared `{at, kind, text}` shape: an\\n`agent_message` item's own text to `message` (confirmed live, issue\\n#41