{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_9","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"findings\":[{\"title\":\"A deleted test file selects no tests, contrary to the approved fail-safe rule\",\"specimen\":\".attavo/bin/select-tests:94\",\"retires\":\"Closes the assumption that every changed test path selects itself; the implementation silently exempts deleted test files.\",\"rejection_test\":\"test_deleted_test_file_selects_itself\",\"severity\":\"Blocking when an item deletes a test file: the selector returns an empty selection instead of the changed test path, so the selected-test gate can pass without detecting the deletion.\"},{\"title\":\"The retired checks command can leak into the executor environment\",\"specimen\":\"attavo/build.py:349\",\"retires\":\"Closes the claim that ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND has left the executor contract, including when the parent process already defines it.\",\"rejection_test\":\"test_build_removes_inherited_attavo_checks_command_from_executor_environment\",\"severity\":\"Blocking when attavo build is launched with ATTAVO_CHECKS_COMMAND already exported: env inherits it and passes it to the adapter and underlying executor, restoring the retired command despite the new contract.\"}],\"tests_named\":[\"test_deleted_test_file_selects_itself\",\"test_build_removes_inherited_attavo_checks_command_from_executor_environment\"]}"}}
